  "recommendation": {
    "word": "hold",
    "why": "Lean proves the variant shows the original's pixel under Reveal and Cont (pixel_eq) and bounds the difference where Reveal fails to 48 px of scroll (drift_window). The breakpoint gate passes on both engines (run 39828600078). The gate compares the pre-flip state only (anchors.json excludes is-pain-dark and the people flip; cells are read at scroll 0); the post-flip look rests on Lean pixel_eq and the pending trajectory pain-dark cell. The toggle frame paints one viewport less in Chromium and the scroll pass paints 28 to 34 percent less area in the WebKit Simulator, but Chromium adds 3 layers and 14 style recalcs and WebKit promotes the stage text block above the animated layer (12 MB more backing while the Pain stage is in view, run 39828605244). The flip-step paint in WebKit is not separable from noise and the flip runs in the UI process only by inference. Hold for the Safari lane (gpu-safari-lane) and the trajectory pain-dark cell (gpu-trajectory-cells, pending)."
